      "chunk_id": "text_11",
      "quote": "We pooled the prevalence around individual outcomes using the double arcsine transformation method. We obtained combined measurements of effect for each primary outcome through metaanalysis under a random-effect model",
      "reason": "The effect measure (prevalence, pooled via double arcsine transformation under a random-effects model) is specified for the outcomes; no other effect measures (e.g., risk ratios) are used since outcomes are prevalences."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_12_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_11",
      "quote": "Statistical heterogeneity was measured through the I 2 statistic and classified as low ( I 2 < 25 % ), moderate ( I 2 25-50 % ), or high ( I 2 > 50 % ).",
      "reason": "Thresholds are reported only for interpreting heterogeneity (I2), not for interpreting the effect size (prevalence magnitude) itself, and no rationale is given."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_12_e3",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "All outcomes are prevalences; no re-expression of results into another effect measure is reported or needed."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_12_e4",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_11",
      "quote": "We obtained combined measurements of effect for each primary outcome through metaanalysis under a random-effect model due to the expected heterogeneity between studies.",
      "reason": "A partial rationale is given (random-effects model chosen due to expected heterogeneity), but the choice of prevalence/double arcsine transformation as the effect measure itself is not explicitly justified."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 85
}

